{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact identifier cutover C+D head 33d1eddf3055ea019a94368d8d4e8bb4f56575de on builder/identifiers-cd-composed-20261112, all 10 artifacts, for request 05d618e2 under promise 9fd2d428 and review request 15f2b78a. The head carries items 1 to 4 of section 8, and the routing, genesis admission, archive and replay changes hold. Three things block it: both browser workflows fail, the B19 store-format fix leaves the race open, and the report misses one dropped kind check and states three facts that the code or the workroom contradicts.\n\nRequired change 1: both browser workflows must pass.\n\n- Card browser scripts, run 43468755112, fails at `packages/mcp/test/views-browser.mjs:241`. The card lists \"Issue 2: TEST second import\" first. `laneRefs` (`apps/views/src/needs-you.ts:34`) sorts lanes by `canonicalize(ref)`, and that line does not change. At main the first key was `inc`, which the stand-in made rise with creation order. At the head the first key is `genesis`, a hash. The product order was arbitrary and stable before and stays so. The assertion assumed creation order. Make it independent of that order, or name the lane that sorts first.\n- Page browser scripts, run 43468755107, times out at `apps/room/page/test/screens.mjs:143` waiting for the heading \"Issues\". `initializeCapture` (`scripts/demo/page-key-custody.ts:88`, `160-163`) writes the settings under `artroom-page:v2`. The page reads only `dap-page-settings-2` (`apps/room/page/src/main.ts:47`), as eed02514 intends, so it opens with no room. `scripts/demo-captures.ts:383-385` and `464-466` use the old key the same way.\n- Main 64112e45 passes both workflows. The gate runs neither script. Cite the runs that pass at the new head.\n\nRequired change 2: the B19 store-format fix must close the race.\n\n- Window 1, `packages/client/src/store-format.ts:68-71`. Process B finds no format file at line 68. Process A then links its word into place at line 79. B lists the directory at line 71, and the listing exempts only `.publishing-*.tmp` names. B counts `.dap-store-format` as a record and refuses the new store as retired. This is the B19 symptom.\n- Window 2, lines 37 and 41. B sees two links, and `publishedLink` at line 37 finds A's temporary name, so B skips the second look. A removes the temporary name at line 85. `publishedLink` at line 41 now returns false, `links` becomes 0, and line 42 refuses the store as retired.\n- One remedy for each: let the listing skip the format file, so B reaches EEXIST and `readWord` at line 88. Call `publishedLink` once and reuse its answer.\n- Witness: force each interleaving. A test that starts two children on an empty directory (`packages/client/test/custody.test.ts:393`) meets the race only by chance. Each witness must fail at 33d1eddf.\n\nRequired change 3: correct the report, `notes/implementation/cd-dropped-kind-checks.md`.\n\n- Add the dropped check in `fitsFieldType` (`packages/bytes/src/field-value.ts:39`): `isScopeRef(v) \u0026\u0026 v.kind === type.kind` became `isScopeRef(v)`. Every act, genesis and slot value passes through it (`derive/src/values.ts:25`, `derive/src/effects.ts:93`). Ruling 429c1be7 makes the drop correct: the kind is checked where the room reads that sequence. Ruling 97583e65 point 7 still requires a row. Name 429c1be7 and the read sites a to d as the replacement. One consequence belongs in the row: a member with `task.control` can now store a Membership reference in the Directory's `task.lane` slot through `open-task` (`platform/src/directory.ts:307`), and main refused that act.\n- \"Anchors and genesis copies\" says this head limits anchors to the register and membership kinds. Only `archive-alias` mode does so (`privatePin` and `#anchoredPrivateName`, `replay/src/verify.ts:87`, `1648-1655`). In the default `retained-name` mode, `#anchor` (`:1603`) and `#privateCopy` (`:1664-1667`) take a caller's anchor of any kind, as main did. Say which mode has the limit. If rulings 5a642337 and 066e49b3 need the limit in both modes, ask the planner before you change the code.\n- The repo-in-ai row of \"Other test changes\" says that no workflow or gate step runs `hosted-loop.test.ts`. Your act e1844d08 and ruling 7bf2c93b show that the plain project `repo-in-ai` in `vitest.projects.mjs` runs it. Correct the row.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- Routing. `routed` (`scope/src/namespace.ts:114-124`) runs first in `deliver` (`object.ts:664`), before judgment and before any write. It compares the stored `this.#store.scope().at.genesis`, never a value the caller sends. `settle` (`core.ts:906`) and `read-wait` (`read-wait.ts:37`) compare stored state the same way, and derive checks again (`delivery.ts:67`). `wrong-incarnation` becomes `wrong-genesis` with the same 409. `genesis-conflict` is an operator incident (`operator.ts:91`).\n- Genesis admission. A foreign read requires `answer.at` to equal `fact.at` and calls `admitSequenceGenesis` (`namespace.ts:470-483`). That function binds the entry hash to `at.genesis` and the seed's scope ID to `at.scope` (`bytes/src/sequence.ts:40-51`). `anchoredCopy` (`replay/src/verify.ts:96-122`) follows a5d65e58: a genesis copy stands only for its own address and its recorded kind.\n- Dropped kind checks. Seventeen rows marked \"the place fixes the kind\" hold in code, among them `derive/src/grant.ts:124`, `platform/src/application-install-reader.ts:20-33`, `scope/src/sessions.ts:149`, `scope/src/site/host.ts:62,80`, `platform/src/reservation-v17.ts:86` and the Directory slots set from applied create results (`directory.ts:279-292`).\n- Births and the archive. Each birth charge comes before its work: `archive-budget.ts:204-208`, `archive-foreign.ts:86`, `116-118`, `140`, `archive-retained.ts:113`, `156`, `168-174` and `archive-input.ts:33`, `41-42`, `69-70`. Nothing deletes a retained birth, so a later use never loses it. One row per sequence (`sqlite.ts:684`), each within `entryBytes`, bounds the growth. Replay admits a served birth with `admitSequenceGenesis` (`verify.ts:1224-1237`), so a different birth reads `incomplete`.\n- `RETIRED_ROOM_READER_COMMIT` (`packages/bytes/src/retired-room.ts:5`) only appears in refusal text. It gates nothing.\n- Canonical admission at `scope/src/core.ts:396`, `platform/src/directory.ts:593` and `platform/src/definition-input.ts:38` follows f2f2a7ea. Rule code of existing platform versions changes in place, which is safe only because every old room retires.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 64112e45 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. Against main, the head changes 924 paths. All of them sit under the 10 artifacts, and all 10 sit at the head. The primary artifact is neither stale nor retired. `git merge-tree` against main is clean, and a merge equals the head.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 285 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-notes` gives one warning: the report is 107,162 bytes, over the 40,960 limit.\n- Seals, on my own clone of the head. `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12, and `security-entry-points.mjs --check` exits 0. `public-release-modules.test.mjs` passes 5 of 5, and `active-source.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12. I ran no other tests.\n- Evidence. All 11 files that the manifest lists match their SHA-256 values, and `SHA256SUMS` verifies. The gate at f9d6fea1 wrote exit 0 and \"gate passed\", on AC power with `powermode 0` at start and end. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep from 11:27 to 11:53. The tree of f9d6fea1 equals `checkpointTree`. From f9d6fea1 to the head, only the manifest, `coverage.json`, the report, the skill and the README change. Attempts 1 to 8 stay failed, and the report claims no pass for them.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A reference names a sequence and nothing more. The kind lives in the admitted genesis and the pinned definition, and the room reads it where it already reads that sequence, as 429c1be7 rules. Routing and admission compare stored geneses. The retired-room stop runs through one answer at each entry point.\n\nSecurity: required change 2 is an availability defect for a local store, and it adds no authority. The `fitsFieldType` drop lets a wrong-kind reference sit in a typed slot. I found no read site that trusts such a slot without its own kind check, but I did not audit all 36 scope-typed platform fields. Two notes for a later head:\n\n1. Timed turns call `#seal` with no fetched facts (`turn.ts:401`), so they retain no births. That holds only if a timed draft never uses a foreign later entry that no earlier entry used. I did not trace `judgeTimed`.\n2. A scope without the opt-in capacity check has no byte cap on retained births, as it had none on retained copies before this head.\n\nSimplification: no required change beyond the three above. The report is 107 KB, well over the notes limit. Its kind table and its seal tables are reference data that a script produced. Moving them to a generated file beside the note would bring the note under the limit.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7bbb29dcbed1b043c06487866ac1f8643f66450e","binding":"assigned","head":"33d1eddf3055ea019a94368d8d4e8bb4f56575de","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1dad5dcfbf1766c6e82ab863a176bdb95ab236de\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40d4b2331c131e497db8eda0be244370f2f27d8b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9fd2d4288ec27d3b459cf8eb99fd4e100a8de08d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40d4b2331c131e497db8eda0be244370f2f27d8b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}